<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>SAZU Protocol</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Serif:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#F1F2ED;
    --surface:#FFFFFF;
    --surface-tint:#E9EAE3;
    --ink:#1E232C;
    --muted:#5B6472;
    --line:#D9DAD1;
    --accent:#B5482F;
    --accent-ink:#7A2F1D;
    --tag-standard-bg:#DCEAE4;
    --tag-standard-fg:#2C5C4C;
    --tag-custom-bg:#F3E1D6;
    --tag-custom-fg:#8A4A1E;
    --mono-bg:#E7E7DF;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(30,35,44,.06);
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
      --bg:#12151A;
      --surface:#1A1E25;
      --surface-tint:#20252D;
      --ink:#E7E8E3;
      --muted:#9AA3AE;
      --line:#2B313B;
      --accent:#E08363;
      --accent-ink:#F2AF95;
      --tag-standard-bg:#1E3730;
      --tag-standard-fg:#7FCBB0;
      --tag-custom-bg:#3A2A1C;
      --tag-custom-fg:#E3A96F;
      --mono-bg:#20242C;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4);
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"]{
    --bg:#12151A;
    --surface:#1A1E25;
    --surface-tint:#20252D;
    --ink:#E7E8E3;
    --muted:#9AA3AE;
    --line:#2B313B;
    --accent:#E08363;
    --accent-ink:#F2AF95;
    --tag-standard-bg:#1E3730;
    --tag-standard-fg:#7FCBB0;
    --tag-custom-bg:#3A2A1C;
    --tag-custom-fg:#E3A96F;
    --mono-bg:#20242C;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4);
  }

  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  body{
    background:var(--bg);
    color:var(--ink);
    font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    line-height:1.6;
    font-size:16px;
  }
  h1,h2,h3{
    font-family:'IBM Plex Serif', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    text-wrap:balance;
    color:var(--ink);
    line-height:1.2;
  }
  code, .mono, .doc-meta, .tag, table, th, td, .rfc{
    font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace;
  }
  a{ color:var(--accent-ink); }
  a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible{
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .shell{
    max-width:1180px;
    margin:0 auto;
    padding: 40px 24px 120px;
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0,760px);
    gap:56px;
    justify-content:center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 920px){
    .shell{ grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); padding:28px 18px 80px; }
    .toc{ display:none; }
    .toc-mobile{ display:block !important; }
  }

  /* ---- doc header (Internet-Draft homage) ---- */
  .doc-header{
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
    padding-bottom:28px;
    margin-bottom:8px;
  }
  .doc-meta{
    display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px 18px;
    font-size:12.5px; color:var(--muted); letter-spacing:.02em;
    margin-bottom:22px;
  }
  .doc-meta span b{ color:var(--ink); font-weight:600; }
  .eyebrow{
    font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent-ink); margin:0 0 10px;
  }
  h1.title{ font-size:clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.7rem); margin:0 0 14px; font-weight:700; }
  .dek{ font-size:1.15rem; color:var(--muted); max-width:60ch; margin:0 0 22px; }
  .abstract{
    background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:6px; padding:20px 22px; box-shadow:var(--shadow);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .abstract p{ margin:0; color:var(--ink); }
  .abstract .label{ font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--muted); display:block; margin-bottom:8px; }

  /* ---- TOC ---- */
  .toc{ position:sticky; top:32px; align-self:start; font-size:13.5px; }
  .toc-title{ font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:12px; }
  .toc ol{ list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; border-left:1px solid var(--line); }
  .toc li{ margin:0; }
  .toc a{
    display:block; padding:6px 0 6px 14px; color:var(--muted);
    text-decoration:none; border-left:2px solid transparent; margin-left:-1px;
  }
  .toc a:hover{ color:var(--ink); border-left-color:var(--accent); }
  .toc-mobile{ display:none; grid-column:1/-1; margin-bottom:8px; }
  .toc-mobile summary{ cursor:pointer; font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); padding:10px 0; }
  .toc-mobile[open] summary{ color:var(--ink); }
  .toc-mobile ol{ list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0 0 12px; columns:2; gap:0 20px; }
  .toc-mobile li{ font-size:13px; padding:4px 0; }
  .toc-mobile a{ color:var(--muted); text-decoration:none; }

  /* ---- main content ---- */
  main{ min-width:0; }
  section{ margin: 52px 0; scroll-margin-top: 24px; }
  section:first-of-type{ margin-top:36px; }
  h2{
    font-size:1.5rem; margin:0 0 18px;
    display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:10px;
  }
  h2 .num{ font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; color:var(--accent); font-size:1rem; font-weight:500; }
  h3{ font-size:1.12rem; margin:28px 0 12px; }
  h3 .num{ font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; color:var(--muted); font-size:.85em; margin-right:8px; }
  p{ margin:0 0 14px; max-width:68ch; }
  ul, ol.plain{ margin:0 0 16px; padding-left:22px; max-width:66ch; }
  li{ margin-bottom:6px; }
  strong{ font-weight:600; }

  .tag{
    display:inline-block; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.04em;
    padding:2px 8px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:500;
    vertical-align:middle;
  }
  .tag.standard{ background:var(--tag-standard-bg); color:var(--tag-standard-fg); }
  .tag.custom{ background:var(--tag-custom-bg); color:var(--tag-custom-fg); }

  .callout{
    border-left:3px solid var(--accent);
    background:var(--surface-tint);
    padding:14px 18px; border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;
    margin:18px 0; max-width:66ch;
  }
  .callout .label{
    font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.1em;
    text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--accent-ink); display:block; margin-bottom:6px;
  }
  .callout p:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }

  .tablewrap{ overflow-x:auto; margin:18px 0 24px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; }
  table{ border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:13px; background:var(--surface); }
  th, td{ text-align:left; padding:10px 14px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); white-space:nowrap; }
  th{ background:var(--surface-tint); font-weight:600; color:var(--muted); font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:.04em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  tr:last-child td{ border-bottom:none; }
  td.wrap, th.wrap{ white-space:normal; }
  td.num{ font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }

  pre{
    background:var(--mono-bg); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px;
    padding:16px 18px; overflow-x:auto; font-size:13px; line-height:1.55;
    margin:16px 0 22px;
  }
  pre code{ background:none; padding:0; }
  code.inline{ background:var(--mono-bg); padding:1px 6px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.88em; }

  .variant-card{
    border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; background:var(--surface);
    padding:22px 24px; margin:20px 0; box-shadow:var(--shadow);
  }
  .variant-head{ display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom:6px; }
  .variant-head h3{ margin:0; }
  .variant-rfc{ font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); }
  .variant-rfc b{ color:var(--ink); }

  hr.rule{ border:none; border-top:1px solid var(--line); margin:56px 0; }

  footer{
    grid-column:1/-1; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding-top:20px; margin-top:20px;
    font-size:12.5px; color:var(--muted);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="shell">
  <header class="doc-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Protocol proposal · split-signing DNSSEC</p>
    <h1 class="title">SAZU</h1>
    <p class="dek"><strong>S</strong>elf-<strong>A</strong>uthenticated <strong>Z</strong>one <strong>U</strong>pdate: a zone owner signs their own zone with DNSSEC keys they keep to themselves, and pushes the signed zone to a DNS hoster. The hoster verifies it and serves it, but never holds a private key. The only credential involved is the DNSSEC key that already signs the zone.</p>
    <div class="doc-meta">
      <span>Status: <b>Draft proposal, v2.0</b></span>
      <span>Scope: <b>Zone owner's signer → hoster's authoritative server</b></span>
      <span>Wire format: <b>RFC 2136 UPDATE + RFC 2931 SIG(0)</b></span>
      <span>Carriers: <b>DNS (TCP/UDP) or the same bytes over HTTPS</b></span>
      <span>Reference implementation: <b><a href="https://github.com/mrwiora/coredns/tree/feat/sazu/plugin/sazu">CoreDNS plugin</a></b></span>
    </div>
    <div class="abstract">
      <span class="label">Abstract</span>
      <p>Today a DNSSEC zone hosted by a third party is either signed by the hoster, which then holds your private key, or signed by you on a &ldquo;hidden primary&rdquo; that the hoster has to pull from with AXFR, which means you run a listening server. SAZU is a third option. The zone owner signs everything offline and pushes the complete signed zone as one standard RFC 2136 dynamic UPDATE, authenticated with SIG(0) using the zone's own DNSSEC key. The hoster checks every signature before it publishes anything. It learns which key to trust from the DS record already in the parent zone, so there is no account, no API token and no shared secret. The one deliberate deviation from existing practice is on the server side. RFC 3007 §4.3 assumes the server re-signs updated data with an online zone key. A SAZU server instead verifies signatures the client supplied and never signs anything itself. <a href="rfc-diff/">rfc-diff/</a> shows that change as a proposed amendment to RFC 3007.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style="max-width:68ch;">
      <span class="label">Why "SAZU"</span>
      <p>Every SAZU message proves its own authorization with the key it carries or references. That covers onboarding (§7), routine pushes (§6) and key rollover (§8). There is no second credential. &ldquo;Self-authenticated&rdquo; describes the mechanism literally.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <details class="toc-mobile">
    <summary>Contents</summary>
    <ol>
{% for number, title, slug in toc %}
      <li><a href="#{{ slug }}">{{ number }}. {{ title }}</a></li>
{% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </details>

  <nav class="toc">
    <p class="toc-title">Contents</p>
    <ol>
{% for number, title, slug in toc %}
      <li><a href="#{{ slug }}">{{ number }}. {{ title }}</a></li>
{% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <main>
{{ sections_html }}
  </main>

  <footer>
    SAZU — Self-Authenticated Zone Update · Draft proposal v2.0
  </footer>
</div>

</body>
</html>
